What this is telling us is that mcaGUI depends on the CRAN package
rgl, and if we look at the web page for that package:

http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rgl/index.html

we see this line:
SystemRequirements:	OpenGL, GLU Library, zlib (optional), libpng
(>=1.2.9, optional), FreeType (optional)

This means, these are system-level packages (not R packages) that R
cannot install for you, but which need to be present.
Sounds like you are using openSuSE. So if you can determine which
packages contain these dependencies, then you can install them with
yast2 or zypper.

It looks like someone else has had a similar problem and a solution here:

http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/Installing-rgl-td865867.html

Since rgl is a CRAN package, this is technically not a Bioconductor
question. So you might want to ask on the R-help mailing list, and/or
contact the rgl maintainer, whose email address is listed here:
http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rgl/index.html

Thanks,
Dan


